<Base title="Affiliate Program — Recommend True Crime That Treats Victims Like People" description="The Cassian Creed affiliate program: a 50% founding commission rate on every title through August 31, 2026, a 40% standing rate after, weekly Gumroad payouts, and conduct terms built on victim dignity and presumption of innocence.">
  <article class="post">
    <p class="evidence evidence--accent">Affiliate Program</p>
    <h1>Recommend true crime that treats victims like people. Get paid for it.</h1>
    <div class="post__content">
      <p>The Cassian Creed affiliate program pays you a commission on every ebook sale you send our way — and holds you to the same standard we hold ourselves: dignity first, accuracy always. Founding affiliates who join now earn our highest rate.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>Cassian Creed is the true-crime imprint of Neural Edge Publishing. Every case file we publish follows one rule above every other: help the victims, and never create new ones. Victims and their families are treated with dignity on every page. We never present an unconvicted person as guilty — "alleged" and "accused" are the law of the house. Every claim is sourced to the record, and we separate what is proven from what is argued from what is inferred. No gratuitous detail — we tell the story; we do not exploit it.</p>
      <p>Our books pair careful human narrative with a clearly labeled analytical layer — A.I. AL, our forensic analysis system — so readers always know what is documented fact and what is independent analysis. Nothing ships without an independent quality and ethics review.</p>
      <p>If your audience trusts you because you cover true crime responsibly, our catalog was built for them.</p>

      <h2>Founding terms — what you earn</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Founding rate: 50% commission on every title in the catalog, through August 31, 2026.</strong> Join during the founding window and the 50% rate applies to all your sales through that date.</li>
        <li><strong>Standing rate: 40% from September 1, 2026 onward.</strong> That is the permanent program rate — stated now so there are no surprises later.</li>
        <li>In plain numbers: at the founding rate, a $5.99 case file pays you about $3.00; the $8.99 two-book bundle pays about $4.50. At the standing rate those become about $2.40 and $3.60. Commissions are one-time and computed on the price the customer actually pays. We do not publish income projections — what you earn depends entirely on your audience, and we will not pretend otherwise.</li>
        <li>Your exact rate appears on your Gumroad affiliate dashboard at approval; that dashboard figure is the binding one.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How tracking and payment work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>30-day cookie.</strong> If a reader clicks your link and buys any time in the next 30 days, you get credit.</li>
        <li><strong>Payouts through Gumroad,</strong> on Gumroad's weekly cycle with a $10 minimum, via direct deposit (US) or PayPal. You will need a free Gumroad account. Refunded purchases are deducted, which is standard.</li>
        <li><strong>Send traffic to the free dossier if you like.</strong> Your link can route to our <a href="/free-dossier/">free case-dossier page</a> — a no-cost first touch for your audience; the 30-day cookie still credits you when they buy later. You can also link directly to any book page.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we approve — and the conduct terms (binding)</h2>
      <p>Approval is manual. We check every applicant by hand against four criteria, drawn from the same internal rule that governs our books:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Victim dignity.</strong> These are real victims and real families. Your coverage treats them as people, not content — no mockery, no gore-bait framing, no exploitation of grief.</li>
        <li><strong>Presumption of innocence.</strong> You never present an unconvicted person as guilty, and you do not run harassment, doxxing, or vigilante campaigns.</li>
        <li><strong>Accuracy.</strong> Your promotion must match what the books actually are — we provide accurate copy to work from, and hype that outruns the record is grounds for removal.</li>
        <li><strong>Audience trust.</strong> A real audience, promoted to honestly: no spam, no deceptive funnels, no misleading claims about price, content, or earnings.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Before live links go out, we ask for a two-line sample blurb — so we both know the representation fits the standard. Violating these terms means immediate link removal. If this describes how you already work, the application takes two minutes. If it does not, this program is not for you, and we say that without apology.</p>

      <h2>Disclosure is required</h2>
      <p>US law (the Federal Trade Commission's endorsement rules) requires you to clearly disclose your affiliate relationship up front — before the link, not buried in a footer. "I earn a commission if you buy through this link" is enough. This is a condition of the program: we spot-check affiliate promotions, and undisclosed promotion is grounds for removal. It protects you, it protects us, and it is the honest thing to do anyway.</p>

      <h2>Where our books are not sold</h2>
      <p>Our catalog is sold through our own store and selected retailers. <strong>We do not sell on Amazon, Kindle Direct Publishing, or Draft2Digital — and affiliates may not promote, list, or imply availability of our titles there.</strong> If you see our books on those platforms, that listing is unauthorized; please tell us.</p>

      <h2>Apply now</h2>
      <p>Signup is self-serve and takes about two minutes. We review every application by hand and respond promptly.</p>
      <p><strong><a href="https://creedcaster5.gumroad.com/affiliates" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Apply at our Gumroad affiliate page →</a></strong></p>
      <p>Questions first? Reach us through the contact information on our <a href="/about/">About page</a> — including for review copies, accurate promotional copy, or audience-fit advice before you apply.</p>
